# surf-app-rerun

Lake Michigan surf map: catalog spots, live NOAA (nearshore wind + offshore waves), surfability scores, Windy embed, email capture, and an admin-gated paid-tier MVP (create a spot anywhere, get a projected verdict). Frontend-first. Prefer a better site over learning scaffolding.

**Full handoff:** read [`CONTEXT.md`](CONTEXT.md) before changing architecture or data. Attach `@CONTEXT.md` in new chats that need the file map.

## Branch

- Work on `dev/rebuild`. Fast refactors are expected.
- `learn/v1` is frozen. Do not commit feature work there.
- `main` is S3 (frontend) + Fly.io (backend) deploy. Do not push there unless asked to ship.

## Data rules

- Wind from nearshore stations only. Waves from offshore buoy allowlist only. Never read WVHT from nearshore.
- Catalog-only selection (~15 km snap) on the public map. Do not restore the backend's legacy location-CRUD endpoints into the UI.
- Do not change scoring thresholds or station allowlists unless asked.

## Run

`cd frontend && npm run dev` — NOAA via Vite proxy, `/api/*` proxied to a local backend on :8000. `cd backend && ADMIN_SECRET=... uvicorn main:app --port 8000` in a second terminal. The backend is in active use — NOAA proxy, email capture, private-spots — not unused; only its original location-CRUD endpoints are legacy and left alone.
